  "result": "Fixed: `remove` was comparing the SKU you pass in against each item's name, so it never matched anything.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` checked `l.item.name != sku`. `remove('sku-1')` was comparing `'sku-1'` with `'Widget'`, so the Widget line was never removed. `add()` already matches on `item.sku`.\n\n**Fix:** changed the check to `l.item.sku != sku`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, meaning only the Gadget line is left.\n- All 6 tests pass. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest`.\n\nNone of the existing tests calls `Cart.remove`, which is how this got through. I can add a regression test if you want one.",
